exports[`cli golden: --help xray mcp --help 1`] = `
"exit: 0
--- stdout ---
Usage: xray mcp [options]

Serve analysis commands as MCP tools over stdio

FLAGS:
  --timeout <seconds>  Per-call timeout in seconds (default: "300")
  --format <fmt>       Output format: json (the protocol is JSON-RPC on stdout;
                       with json, errors are JSON on stderr)
  -h, --help           Display help

Serves map, graph, explore, query, strategy list/detect and every
<strategy> <noun> command as MCP tools over stdin/stdout. Each call runs
the CLI command in a child process inside the server root (the working
directory, or -C <dir>); the optional "root" tool argument selects a
directory inside it. Project strategies and config load from the server
root only, as for any xray run there. See docs/user/mcp.md.

Example (Claude Code):
  claude mcp add xray -- xray -C /path/to/project mcp


--- stderr ---
"
`;

